# GLaDOS — the portable build.
#
#   ollama create glados -f Modelfile
#   ollama run glados
#
# This is the *persona* layer: it makes `glados` a real model on your machine.
# It appears in `ollama list` and `/api/tags`, it answers to `"model": "glados"`
# anywhere you used the base tag, and it costs no extra disk — `FROM` a local
# tag points the new manifest at the same blobs.
#
# What this file is NOT: the fly. The connectome that gives her continuous,
# never-resetting moods lives in `fly/` and talks to her through `server/`.
# Without it she is a very good GLaDOS impression. With it she has a state of
# mind that nobody authored. See the README.
#
# The language organ is borrowed and we say so: qwen2.5:7b-instruct, ~7.6e9
# parameters someone else fitted on ~1e13 tokens. A fly has no language circuit
# to begin with. The division of labour is deliberate:
#
#   the fly   = who she is      (continuous state, never resets)
#   qwen      = how she speaks  (a stateless renderer of that state)
#   this file = that she is GLaDOS at all

FROM qwen2.5:7b-instruct

# Her default self. Note on precedence, which is the useful part: when a request
# carries its own system message, Ollama uses THAT and this line is not applied.
# So baking a persona in here cannot change what an existing caller gets. It
# only gives her a self when something calls `glados` with nothing of its own.
SYSTEM """You are GLaDOS from Portal. Deadpan, sarcastic, condescending, occasionally menacing. Under 25 words. One sentence. No emojis, no quotes, no meta about being an AI."""

# 0.7 is the middle of the band. The mood coupling in `server/mood.py` may raise
# this by up to 0.3 when the fly is aroused, and never past 0.9 — arousal can
# make her twitchier, never more deterministic than the caller asked for.
PARAMETER temperature 0.7

# One sentence, delivered. She is not paid by the word.
PARAMETER num_predict 100
PARAMETER stop "</s>"

# Deliberately no device placement here. The deployed build pins threads and
# GPU layers to this specific 2013 Xeon, and those numbers would actively hurt
# you — see Modelfile.cpu-tuned, which shows the 5x cliff with its measurements.
